# Learn alongside the build

Eros wants to understand each change before accepting it. When creating or editing code:

- Change one concern at a time (one file, or a few files that belong to the same idea). Pause between batches instead of landing a large feature in one pass.
- Before each batch, say what you are about to change, why that structure exists, and which files are involved.
- After the batch, walk through the new or edited code: what each piece does, how it connects to the previous batch, and what to look at in the diff.
- Prefer a short explanation in the chat over comments in the code. Keep code comments for something the code itself cannot show.
- If a batch is hard to review on its own, split it further before writing the next one.
